\b What you are installing\b0\par
\par
SpellVision, the worker that runs it, and the ComfyUI 0.34.0 engine this release was proven against. Node packs that engine needs are included. Model files are not.\par
\par
\b ComfyUI is pinned to this build\b0\par
\par
This installer does not fetch a newer ComfyUI, and it will not heal a ComfyUI you replace by hand. The graphs SpellVision builds assume the node names in this pinned 0.34.0 tree. A later release is planned to adopt a newer engine on its own. Until then, updating Comfy from inside Comfy, or swapping the folder, is unsupported.\par
\par
\b Models are a separate decision\b0\par
\par
Checkpoints, VAEs, text encoders, CLIP-vision models, and LoRAs are not in this box. First launch asks you to choose a model library. Nothing is downloaded until you ask.\par
\par
About 30 GB of disk is required after unpack. The figure on the folder page includes the engines and the space the unpack needs. It does not include your models.\par
\par
\b Licences\b0\par
\par
SpellVision is Apache-2.0. The text ships as licenses\SpellVision-Apache-2.0.txt.\par
\par
Qt 6.10.2 is LGPL-3.0, linked dynamically so you can replace the Qt DLLs beside SpellVision.exe. The licence text ships as licenses\Qt-LGPL-GPL.txt. Corresponding source is at https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/6.10/6.10.2/single/.\par
\par
ComfyUI 0.34.0 is GPL-3.0. SpellVision does not link it. It talks to it over HTTP on this machine, with Comfy's own Python. The licence text ships as licenses\ComfyUI-GPL-3.0.txt.\par
\par
The aggregate notice is NOTICE, next to SpellVision.exe.\par
\par
Accepting continues the install of that pinned engine, without models. Cancel leaves the machine unchanged.\par
